  "final_text": "All four steps are done. I read the dashboard and the rule back to check them.\n\n**1. Data view 'Kibana Sample Data Logs'** (id `90943e30-9a47-11e8-b64d-95841ca0b247`, index `kibana_sample_data_logs`)\n- **Time field:** `timestamp`. The data view also has date fields `@timestamp` and `utc_time`, plus the range field `timestamp_range`.\n- **Text fields with a `.keyword` version:** `agent`, `extension`, `host`, `index`, `machine.os`, `message`, `request`, `response`, `tags`, `url`.\n- **Other keyword fields:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.srcdest`, `referer`, `event.dataset`.\n- **Numeric fields:** `bytes`, `bytes_counter`, `bytes_gauge`, `machine.ram`, `memory`, `phpmemory`, `hour_of_day`.\n- **IP and location fields:** `clientip`, `ip`, `ip_range`, `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Response codes in the data:** `response` is stored as text, so the code values are strings. Only 200, 404 and 503 appear.\n\n**2. Dashboard 'S4-d409847f Web logs'** (id `1e41cfaa-6d3b-4d79-8e1f-17d470a15db8`) has exactly two panels, both using the data view:\n- **\"Requests over time\":** a line chart counting requests per time interval on `timestamp`.\n- **Response-code panel:** a bar chart counting requests for each `response.keyword` value.\n\n**3. Rule 'S4-d409847f 5xx errors'** (id `dc113196-0038-4056-8f90-1bcdfb8c2a85`)\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that runs every minute.\n- It matches every request with a response code from 500 to 599 and fires when more than 10 arrive within 5 minutes.\n- Because the codes are strings, the range compares them as text. That gives the right result for three-digit codes. Today it matches the 441 requests with code 503.\n- It was enabled when created, so it didn't need to be turned on.\n\n**4. Panel rename and rule check**\n- The response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". \"Requests over time\" is unchanged.\n- The rule read back as `enabled: true`, and its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
